{"title":"Career Roadmap · Paramedic","role":"Paramedic","summary":"A Paramedic is an emergency-care professional trained to provide rapid assessment, stabilization, emergency treatment, and safe transportation of patients before and during transfer to definitive medical care.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Emergency & Trauma Care Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Paramedic is an emergency-care professional trained to provide rapid assessment, stabilization, emergency treatment, and safe transportation of patients before and during transfer to definitive medical care."},{"type":"p","text":"Paramedics may work in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ambulance services"},{"text":"Emergency medical services (EMS)"},{"text":"Emergency departments"},{"text":"Trauma centres"},{"text":"Disaster-response teams"},{"text":"Industrial emergency services"},{"text":"Event medical services"},{"text":"Air/critical-care transport, with additional training"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The role can involve:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Emergency assessment"},{"text":"Airway and breathing support"},{"text":"Cardiovascular assessment"},{"text":"CPR and resuscitation"},{"text":"Trauma management"},{"text":"Patient stabilization"},{"text":"Emergency medications within authorized scope"},{"text":"Splinting and immobilization"},{"text":"Patient transport"},{"text":"Handover to hospital teams"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Scope of practice varies by jurisdiction, qualification, employer and EMS protocols. A graduate should verify the applicable registration, certification and medication/procedure authority before practicing independently."}]},{"heading":"Recommended Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Emergency & Trauma Care Technology Degree","Clinical / EMS Internship","Ambulance + Emergency Department